Anomaly alert emails required manual triggering from the web UI. Now any anomalous reading inserted by the ESP32 automatically dispatches the alert to all registered users.

## Changes

### `model/ConsumoModel.php`
- Added `getDeviceZScore(int $device_id, float $consumo_raw, int $lookback_days = 30): ?float` — queries 30-day `AVG`/`STDDEV` for the device and returns the z-score of the incoming raw value; returns `null` when data is insufficient (no rows or σ = 0)

### `insert_consumo.php`
- After a successful insert, computes z-score of the new reading via `getDeviceZScore()`
- If z-score ≥ 2.0, acquires an exclusive `flock` on a temp lock file, re-checks a **1-hour global cooldown**, then sends the full device anomaly report (`getAnomalies('device', 30, 2.0)`) to every address returned by `UserModel::getAllEmails()`
- Cooldown timestamp is written only after a successful send
- All email errors are caught and logged; the sensor JSON response is never affected

```php
$z_score = $model->getDeviceZScore($id_dispositivo, $consumo_raw);

if ($z_score !== null && $z_score >= 2.0) {
    $lock_file = fopen($anomaly_cooldown_file . '.lock', 'c');
    if ($lock_file && flock($lock_file, LOCK_EX)) {
        // re-check cooldown under lock, then send to all users
    }
}
```

The email content and thresholds are identical to the manual flow in the anomalies web module.

Implements the frontend communication layer for Network Topology Builder (PR #3 of the roadmap) — pure types and API service, no UI components.

## New files

- **`frontend/src/types/networkTopology.types.ts`** — types strictly matched to the backend entity:
  - `NodeType`, `NodeSourceType`, `ConnectionTechnology` union types
  - `TopologyNode` (with optional `metadata?: Record<string, unknown>` from entity), `TopologyConnection`, `NetworkTopology`
  - `id: string` (UUID) — matched to `@PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')` on the entity
  - `CreateNetworkTopologyDto` / `UpdateNetworkTopologyDto`, plus typed API response wrappers

- **`frontend/src/services/networkTopology.service.ts`** — 7-method class consuming existing `{ api }` from `./api`:

```typescript
networkTopologyService.getLatest(contractId, subsystemIndex)   // → NetworkTopology | null
networkTopologyService.getById(id)                             // → NetworkTopology | null (404 → null)
networkTopologyService.getAllByContract(contractId)            // → NetworkTopology[]
networkTopologyService.create(dto)                             // → NetworkTopology
networkTopologyService.save(contractId, subsystemIndex, dto)   // → NetworkTopology (immutable versioning via PUT)
networkTopologyService.getHistory(contractId, subsystemIndex, page?, limit?)
networkTopologyService.delete(contractId, subsystemIndex)      // soft-delete
```

`getLatest` and `getById` absorb 404s and return `null`; all other errors propagate. Follows the singleton `export default new Service()` pattern used across the frontend service layer.

